#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.13"
# dependencies = ["rich>=13.0.0", "pytermstyle"]
#
# [tool.uv.sources]
# # A commit rather than a tag, for the reason `pull-requests` gives at length:
# # uv re-resolves a mutable ref against the remote on every run, which costs
# # over a second and fails outright with no network. That commit is v0.1.1.
# pytermstyle = { git = "https://github.com/datapointchris/pytermstyle", rev = "bef61a95120df523758029eac6692898140e4262" }
# ///
"""Pick one of your open PRs, from anywhere, and open its diff to read.

    prs              pick one and open it in a tmux window
    prs list         print them instead, one row each

Enter on a row opens the action menu. A letter takes that action there and then,
without the menu, and the footer names them — `m` is merge, which is the one
worth pressing from the list, since the confirm it prints is the whole flow.

The menu shows the PR's description rendered as markdown, and its own footer names
the keys that scroll it. `p` fetches GitHub's own rendering instead, with the
comment threads the listing does not carry, and `r` opens a Claude window running
`/review-pr` on it.

Lives in dotfiles rather than in fleet because every machine has this and only
some have fleet. The data comes from `pull-requests`, the one place that knows how to
ask a provider for PRs; this is the renderer, the picker and the window.

Fetches, never checks out. `gh pr checkout` switches branches, which aborts
outright when the repo has uncommitted work and disturbs it when it does not —
for reading, that is all cost. Check it out yourself to run the code.

nvim listens on a socket so a Claude split into the window can be asked what is
under the cursor. That session did not write the code, which is exactly why it
is the right one to ask.

Python rather than shell because the work here is arithmetic: measuring cells,
padding columns and coloring them. The previous version did that in jq inside a
heredoc, where there is no padding primitive and a string repeated zero times
comes back as null. fzf is still the picker — it is the picker everywhere else on
this machine, and a reimplementation would be a worse one that also had to be
maintained.
"""

